AUDIO: 'MiniMax H3 is one of the best, if not the best, open video models out there right now. It\'s already incredible with face consistency, motion coherence, and overall quality. But what if I told you there\'s a single Laura that can push it'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'even further, making faces hyper-realistic, skin pore level detailed, and expressions that actually hold up in extreme close-ups? This is the MiniMax H3 Realism People Laura by Fall. And today, we\'re not just talking'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'about it, we\'re testing it head-to-head against the base model inside ComfyUI. Same seeds, same prompts, same settings. The only difference? This tiny adapter. Let\'s jump in.'

[00:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'All right, so we\'re inside ComfyUI right now. If you\'ve used MiniMax H3 before, this node setup will look familiar. For this first test, we\'re doing reference to video, but keep in mind, this Laura'

[00:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'works across all three modes: text-to-video, image-to-video, and reference-to-video. Here\'s our node setup. We\'re using the MiniMax H3 reference-to-video model.'

[01:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Sampler is set to res, multi-step, simple at 20 steps. I\'m intentionally not using Sage attention or any turbo or speed optimizations for this first run. I want the absolute best quality so we can'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'judge the Laura fairly. Resolution is locked at 1.6 megapixels, which lands us right around 720p HD. Now, the prompt. The trigger word for this Laura is R34L1SM.'

[01:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'That\'s realism with numbers, and you want it right at the start of your prompt. Here\'s what I wrote. R34L1SM subject definition, the woman shown in the picture, preserve exact facial'

[01:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'features, photorealistic live-action 10-second video, sitting at a dining table, she picks up the spoon from the ramen bowl in front of her, uses the a to taste the broth. A quick tip on prompting, specificity is'

[01:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
